<section class="content">

<h2>Catechist Guide</h2>
<p class="big-question">To prepare and lead the lesson. For catechist use only.</p>

<h3>Lesson Summary</h3>

<p><strong>Estimated duration:</strong> 50-60 minutes (with activities, 90 minutes)</p>
<p><strong>Central theme:</strong> Holy Orders is the sacrament through which Christ, the Supreme and Eternal High Priest, prolongs his ministry through men configured with him in three degrees: bishop, priest, and deacon.</p>
<p><strong>Objectives:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>That the student understands the three degrees of Holy Orders and the difference between the common and ministerial priesthood.</li>
<li>That they discover the biblical roots of the priesthood, from Melchizedek to the Last Supper.</li>
<li>That they appreciate the profound meaning of celibacy and the mission of the priest.</li>
<li>That they awaken or renew their appreciation for the priests in their lives and pray for vocations.</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Key Scripture verse:</strong> John 15:16 (&laquo;You did not choose me, but I chose you&raquo;)</p>
<p><strong>Catechism references:</strong> CCC 1533-1600</p>

</section>

