<h3>Additional Resources</h3>
<ul>
<li><strong>YouCat 248-259:</strong> Accessible explanation of Holy Orders in youth language.</li>
<li><strong>Francis Trochu:</strong> <em>The Cur&eacute; of Ars</em>. Classic biography, highly readable, full of anecdotes.</li>
<li><strong>Saint Josemar&iacute;a:</strong> Homily &laquo;A Priest Forever&raquo; in <em>Loving the Church</em>. Free online.</li>
<li><strong>Ascension Presents:</strong> Fr. Mike Schmitz, videos on the priesthood.</li>
<li><strong>Real + True (OSV):</strong> Episode on Holy Orders at osvnews.com.</li>
<li><strong>Scott Hahn:</strong> <em>Rome Sweet Home</em>, testimony of a Protestant pastor who discovered the Catholic priesthood.</li>
<li><strong>Hakuna Group Music:</strong> &laquo;Tuyo soy&raquo; (&laquo;I Am Yours&raquo;), a vocational hymn.</li>
<li><strong>Gregorian chant:</strong> <em>Tu es Sacerdos in aeternum</em> (Ps 110:4), sung at ordinations.</li>
</ul>

</section>

<section class="content">

<h3>Catechist's Prayer</h3>

<blockquote>
<p>Lord Jesus, Supreme and Eternal High Priest,<br />
who at the Last Supper gave your apostles<br />
the power to perpetuate your sacrifice of love,<br />
I pray for the men you have called<br />
and will call to ordained ministry.<br />
Sustain the bishops in their mission as shepherds,<br />
the priests in their faithful service,<br />
the deacons in their witness of charity.<br />
And grant me, catechist, the grace<br />
to speak of this sacrament with reverence, truth, and love,<br />
so that my words may kindle in others<br />
gratitude and generosity.<br />
Amen.</p>
</blockquote>

</section>

